    <<link "Continue" "R5_Bathroom">><</link>>
</div>

:: R5_Bathroom [r5 story intimate]
<<scene "Executive Washroom, Floor 39" "files/images/mood/r5-bathroom-mirror.png">>
<<objective "Get the bra on before anyone arrives.">>

The executive washroom has three stalls and a lock on the main door. I engage the lock. The click echoes off tile that probably cost more per square foot than my first apartment.

I set the box on the counter next to the soap dispenser. Pull off my jacket and hang it on the back of the door. Unknot my tie. Start unbuttoning my shirt.

Here is the thing about undressing in a corporate bathroom at 7:15 in the morning: every sound is an indictment. The shirt fabric sliding off my shoulders. The clink of my belt buckle. The rustle of tissue paper as I lift the bra out and hold it up under the fluorescent light.

It weighs nothing. A few ounces of fabric and wire and engineering designed to do one thing, which is hold breasts I don't have against a chest that's never needed holding. The straps are adjustable. The band has three rows of hooks. The cups have the faintest padding, a thin layer of foam that would smooth the contour of real tissue against clothing. On me it will create a silhouette that doesn't exist. A ghost of shape over flat skin and the hard line of my sternum.

I unclasp it. Slide my arms through the straps. Reach behind my back and fumble with the hooks.

The fumble is what kills me. I can't do it. My fingers are shaking and the hooks are small and the angle is wrong. I've watched Lena do this ten thousand times, that quick blind reach behind the back, the snap of connection, the slight adjustment of the band. She does it the way I tie my shoes. Muscle memory. Thoughtless.

It takes me four attempts. On the fourth try the hooks catch and the band tightens across my ribcage and the straps settle onto my shoulders.

Weight. Not much, but present. The straps create two parallel lines of gentle pressure running from my collarbones to the band in back. When I move my arms, the straps shift. When I breathe deep, the band tightens. When I look down, the cups sit against my chest like hands cupping nothing, holding the space where something might eventually be.

<<modstat "feminization" 5>>

I button my shirt over it. Straighten the collar. Knot the tie. Check the mirror.

Same face. Same jaw. Same hair combed the same way it's been combed since I was nineteen and my father told me to stop looking like a teenager. The shirt sits flat. The bra is invisible. You could pat me on the chest and feel nothing except maybe the faintest ridge of the underwire if you pressed hard enough and knew what you were pressing for.

But I know it's there. I can feel the straps with every breath. The band around my ribs, a constant low hug. The cups against my skin, holding their empty promise and below, the panties. The lace against my cock, the silk against my ass. Two layers now. A matching set.

I stare at the mirror and try to find the man my father raised. He's still there, technically. Same bones, same suit, same polished shoes. But he's wearing a bra and panties under the uniform and the uniform is starting to feel like the costume, not the other way around.

I pick up the box and the tissue paper, fold them flat, and slide them into my briefcase. Check the lock. Unlock the door. Walk back to my office.

The straps move with every step. I count seventeen steps to my office door. Each one registers at the shoulders and the chest and the hips. Each one whispers.

